## Key notes for the Cloudflare Workers port

1. **`node:crypto`** — replace `createHash("sha256")` with `crypto.subtle.digest("SHA-256", ...)` (async), `randomBytes` with `crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(n))`, `generateKeyPairSync("ed25519")` with `crypto.subtle.generateKey({ name: "Ed25519" }, true, ["sign"])`. `timingSafeEqual` can be replaced with a constant-time comparison using `crypto.subtle.timingSafeEqual` or a manual XOR loop.

2. **`node:fs` / `node:path`** — `readSkillMarkdown` and `listAvailableSkills` must be rewritten. The five known Paperclip skills should be inlined as TypeScript string constants at build time.

3. **`node:dns/promises`** and **`node:http`/`node:https`** — The `resolveInviteResolutionTarget` + `probeInviteResolutionTarget` subsystem (used only by `GET /invites/:token/test-resolution`) needs to be replaced with `fetch()` and the DNS resolution parts either dropped or approximated.

4. **`logger`** — must be replaced with the Workers-compatible logger already in the Hono app.

5. **`db.transaction()`** — the `FOR UPDATE` advisory lock queries inside the member-update handlers use raw SQL with `tx.execute(sql\`...\`)`; these will work with Drizzle + postgres-js via Hyperdrive, but note `FOR UPDATE` has no effect in autocommit mode.

6. **`opts` (deploymentMode/Exposure/bindHost/allowedHostnames)** — the `accessRoutes` factory takes these as constructor arguments. In the Worker, these will come from `env` bindings.
